<title>USA: AT&amp;T's Allen leaves hospital.</title>
<headline>AT&amp;T's Allen leaves hospital.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>AT&amp;T Corp Chairman and Chief Executive Robert Allen on Tuesday left the hospital after undergoing surgery for a faulty heart valve last week.</p>
<p>Allen, 62, returned to his New Jersey home to convalesce after surgery in Rochester, Minnesota on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;He is looking forward to returning to work by the end of the month,&quot; an AT&amp;T spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>In his absence Chief Operating Officer and CEO-designate John Walter is running AT&amp;T. Walter is formally slated to become chief executive in May 1998.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsrom 212 859 1610))</p>
